<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 175 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 175 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 175 million stg of assistance at established interest rates after revising its money market shortage to 1.6 billion stg.</p>
<p>The Bank allotted 121 million stg in bills outright and 54 million stg in repos to June 16 and 17. That leaves a residual shortage of 150 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
